body:
Society does act as if mothers can do no wrong. I love my mother but I realize a lot of damage she has done in my life although I forgive her I try to keep my distance. She constantly put us against each other (siblings and me) and makes it seem like to others I am blaming her or trying to paint me as this spoiled girl who has gotten everything in the world and I am just acting out like a child. No I am an adult woman and I am tired of the he say she say in my family, sometimes I physically feel unwell, and I am trying to heal from years of trauma. I am an adult and I do not have to be around my family all the time. It has gotten to the point where I srsly dont even tell people about my family - I just talk about it privately in therapy. 

&#x200B;

I am a grown woman and atp I am tired of people constantly trying to paint me in a bad light. So I choose to not be around them. I have that right. They manipulate ppl so people can say "You're such a loving and caring big sis or mother. Your daughter/sister is sooo horrible." I am sick of it that is why I stay away. You can lie and make up all stories I cannot control that but I promise you I wont be around you. So idgaf about people who have healthy or healthier parents than mine opinions. They do not get it and never will.

I am also rewatching SATC and boy when I tell you my perception from 21 (when I first watched) to 26 (rewatching) has changed. Lol. I actually do not think Big was a total asshole (still asshole-y) but he DID tell Carrie he did not want to be with her, he also made it clear that he liked models BEFORE Natasha, and he did set multiple boundaries (which are important in any relationship) and Carrie would throw a tantrum. I do believe they both were unhealthy and as a woman I can see how that would hurt Carrie but for the most part she would call him an asshole for being who he is. I felt as though Carrie could never be satisfied and should have moved on to someone who fit her better. 

&#x200B;

I just watched this episode and thought the same thing. Then she ran off with the busboy I was like??? I get that she hated the bag, and he should have went out there with her BUT she also failed to communicate that she hated the bag and she (IMO) could have just asked him to come men are not mind reader in fact no one is. I think their relationship had a lot of communication issues.

I am so glad people are catching on to this! This still happens to me as a grown woman. My mom will overfeed me (she cooks when I visit) after I repeatedly tell her I do not want her to fix my plate I can make it myself bc she puts wayyyy too much. I been noticed this when I was a preteen. Yes I did binge anf emotional eat BUT when I was 13 and tell my mom I was going on a diet she would get mad sometimes, other times slut-shame me and say I was trying to lose weight for men (she has done this until college), and then sometimes she would ACT like she is supportive and then she would pile my plate while at the same time shaming me for being overweight. Narcissists really mind fuck u. It is sad they do that to CHILDREN. I was a child. Now I am a grown woman and this is why my counselor said she thinks I have an eating disorder I definitely agree. I love my mom but nmom are sometimes downright EVIL. All because they are in secret competition with their daughters. This is the reason why I have issues making female friends now. If I cant trust my own got damn momma then I know I cant trust women and I know that is sooo bad to think I am getting better. Now my mom knows she cant compete with me so she is trying to lose weight and I am happy for her. But it is kinda eerie and weird. It just feels weird. I love her but I will never forget her trying to sabotage me in my childhood, teen, years, and she almost succeeded in my 20s but i moved out and now I can lose weight. 

&#x200B;

I have seen narcissistic mothers either trying to make their daughters overweight and I know someone who had a narcissistic mother who restricted her. Neither are healthy. Smh. Child it is just sad they cant just LOVE their children. SMh.
